{
  "_doc": "Capability table. Each model lists the effort values its route accepts and, per effort, [Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index v4.3.2, AA cost per index task in US$ at list price], read 2026-10-28 from artificialanalysis.ai/leaderboards/models; values marked in `estimated` were interpolated from the same model's other rungs. `adjust` shifts ability for one kind of work, from the vendor and leaderboard evidence in docs/ALGORITHM.md. Input types come from models.dev at run time, with `inputs` (a models.dev snapshot of 2026-10-28) as the offline fallback; context comes from models.dev only. Models dominated on both price and score (claude-haiku-4-5, kimi-k3, deepseek-v4-pro, gpt-6-sol) are left out on purpose: a route serving them shows them as unrated. `default_adjust` applies to every model without its own value for that kind: only Grok has native X search, listed in its `tools`; a task that needs X posts goes only to a model with `x_search` when one is reachable. `decider_scale` maps the local decider's difficulty score onto the 0-4 levels (offset, scale), fitted by bench/decider.py on its 30 labelled tasks for pplx-decider-flash-v1.2; refit it there for another decider.",
